ee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Многие великие мысли подобны кузнечным мехам: они надувают и делают ещё более пустым.","en":"Many great thoughts are like smiths’ bellows: they inflate and make emptier still."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-993c30d9c923cd967bd002f8ef995281","tos.text-unit.sid-993c30d9c923cd967bd002f8ef995281"]},"form":"thut","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-96f0649578b9adcd7b17daaf08c5bc47","tos.text-unit.sid-96f0649578b9adcd7b17daaf08c5bc47"]},"form":"thun","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["memory","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра предостерегает от несправедливости к отшельникам: им трудно забыть и отплатить.","en":"Zarathustra warns against wronging hermits: it is hard for them to forget or repay."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-4cac792ccb0b9dd8af79db2ae8dcab71","tos.text-unit.sid-4cac792ccb0b9dd8af79db2ae8dcab71"]},"form":"Thatet","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.21","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-4d619a94ef7199cfd4aaf7202d99a625","tos.text-unit.sid-4d619a94ef7199cfd4aaf7202d99a625"]},"form":"thäte","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"marriage-questioner","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["becoming","necessity","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Тот, кто искал служанку с добродетелями ангела, сам стал служанкой женщины.","en":"The man who sought a servant with the virtues of an angel himself became a woman’s servant."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-39e6ff60031ed553461fb31249d8b890","tos.text-unit.sid-39e6ff60031ed553461fb31249d8b890"]},"form":"thun","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.23","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6fd7755f1e82fc19a7c3aede2f65e2fc","tos.text-unit.sid-6fd7755f1e82fc19a7c3aede2f65e2fc"]},"form":"thun","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.01","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-048901ec9c49143f8e2c18239ac533b5","tos.text-unit.sid-048901ec9c49143f8e2c18239ac533b5"]},"form":"thun","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"animals","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["bestowing-virtue","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Возвращаясь к друзьям и врагам, Заратустра снова может говорить, дарить и делать добро возлюбленным.","en":"Returning to friends and enemies, Zarathustra can speak, give, and do good to his beloved again."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-dd4549d204c95af0458c76a477cfa443","tos.text-unit.sid-dd4549d204c95af0458c76a477cfa443"]},"form":"thut","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["becoming","identity","necessity","creation","redemption","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Созидание облегчает жизнь, но созидающий должен перенести страдания и многие превращения.","en":"Creating lightens life, but the creator must undergo suffering and many transformations."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.03","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-85d7122851043c5befd3b26ec46e61fa","tos.text-unit.sid-85d7122851043c5befd3b26ec46e61fa"]},"form":"thun","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"source-use","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sp